# The wall clock.
#
#   .now()     seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC, a float, where the platform has a clock that knows the date (tag clock); a platform
#              that has none raises a `system` error. .pc() is the clock for measuring and starts at 0.

@ time.now-is-a-float core clock float
> x::.now()
> x>1700000000.0
= 1

@ time.now-moves-forward core clock float
> a::.now()
> b::.now()
> ~b<a
= 1

@ time.now-is-not-the-process-clock core clock float
> .now()>.pc()
= 1
